From 6024aa6a8de7f072f2ce4cc60e9323c940ab3a60 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dimitry B <dimitryB@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 1 Nov 2026 18:21:59 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] eip155: search after any failed send no node answered, within
 the budget

The lookup still reported a mined settlement as failed in three ways.

A fast failure got one lookup. A gateway can forward the transaction
and answer 5xx, or drop the connection, in under 10 s, and that is no
more a rejection than a timeout is. Only a node's own JSON-RPC answer
now skips the search.

The 3 s lookup limit hid a transaction from RPCs that answer in more
than 3 s but under the 10 s request limit. The limit is now 8 s.

The search did not count against the send's budget, so a failing send
ran past the SDK's 90 s. It now ends with the budget. A send that fails
can still run one round of lookups over, but it has no hash to lose.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 .../x402-chain-eip155/src/chain/provider.rs   | 72 ++++++++++++++-----
 1 file changed, 54 insertions(+), 18 deletions(-)

